OL,3,GNEWSABride's veil saved by rower after
OL,4,Ait blows away
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt is traditional for someone to catch
OL,7,Fthe bride's bouquet at a wedding, but
OL,8,Fon Friday a group of rowers managed to
OL,9,Fcatch the veil after it blew into a
OL,10,Friver.
OL,12,FTina and Steve Appleford had just tied
OL,13,Fthe knot and were taking group photos
OL,14,Fby the River Great Ouse in Bedford when
OL,15,Fthe wind whipped the veil away.
OL,17,F"My husband ducked because he thought
OL,18,Fit was a bird going past his head, then
OL,19,Fwe realised it was actually my veil,"
OL,20,Frecalled Tina, 54, who comes from
OL,21,FBurton Latimer, Northamptonshire.
OL,23,APub: 21-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,373,370,200,160,0,100
